something killed, `cmp' then shows the totalexperience points of the player instead of the gained experience points.Now that I understand this, it's much easier for me to use the tag.  I dobelieve, however, that resetting the compare value to current XP instead of0 at login would be beneficial.Thanks again,        Kairon**sauron**To: cashimor Re:   Experience/levelsDate: Aug  1Well, to try and answer your questions, the exp tables in the guild masterwill be obsolete, but I think that the new funs I've added to player.c willdo the job you want.1. query_min_exp_for_level() - this returns the minimum exp a player should                               have for their current level.2. query_exp_for_next_level() - this returns the exp required for the next                                level.3. query_exp_to-advance() - this returns the actual amount of exp that the                            player needs to advance (ie the target exp minus                            the current exp). hence 0 means that they are                            ready to advance4. query_perc_exp_to_advance() - this does the same as the last fun, except                                 it converts the value into a percentage.5. calculate_exp_for_level() - pass this a level and it will return the                               amount of exp required for that level - I                               can add guild dependent factors into the fun                               if need be.Let me know if these don't cover what you want for the tag and I'll seewhat I can do.Dave**quasimodo**To: cashimorRe:   Bug reportDate: Apr 20It was at the eastern room on the main village road. There is a diggable sandIn the sand I was at the bottom of shaft and did 'dig south'. The messageI reported appears - just after them I went up from the hole afraid of gamecrash. All.**madmax**To: cashimorSubj: illegal killDate: Jun  2i got killed by smolrlok wihtout 